{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (93.1%) to Cathelicidin-PY K:17%; R: 10%; L:14%, I=L=A:7%. Mol Wt: 3361.028; GRAVY: -0.53; Mol Formula: C151H264N46O39; mol ex coeff: 0. Activity: slightly less active than the WT. active against E. coli ATCC 25922 (MIC 1 uM), P. aeruginosa SVB-B9 (MIC 4 uM) in MHB, S-aureus ATCC 29213 (MIC>64 uM), and C-albicans SC5314T (MIC >64 uM). Antimicrobial robustness: salt-sensitive; active against E. coli ATCC 25922 (MIC 4 uM), P. aeruginosa SVB-B9 (MIC 32 uM) in cation-adjusted MHB media. Structure: less helical than WT. UPdated 6/2023", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "36838983", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Molecules. 2023 Feb 20;28(4):1993. doi: 10.3390/molecules28041993. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03600", "source_id": "AP03600", "source_numeric_id": "03600", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03600", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Flow-Based Fmoc-SPPS Preparation and SAR Study of Cathelicidin-PY Reveals Selective Antimicrobial Activity.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (93.1%) to Cathelicidin-PY K:21%; L:14%; R: 10%. Peptide engineering: the orginal disulfide bond between C3 and C7 has been replaced with a amide bond between the sidechains of D3 and X7 (2,4-diaminobutyric acid. Warning: represented with K in this sequence). Activity: active against E. coli ATCC 25922 (1 uM), P. aeruginosa SVB-B9 (MIC 8 uM) in MHB, S-aureus ATCC 29213 (MIC>64 uM), and C-albicans SC5314T (MIC >64 uM). Antimicrobial robustness: salt-sensitive; active against E. coli ATCC 25922 (4 uM), P. aeruginosa SVB-B9 (MIC 32 uM) in cation-adjusted MHB media. Structure: more helical than WT. Most helical in TFE in the series!", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "36838983", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Molecules. 2023 Feb 20;28(4):1993. doi: 10.3390/molecules28041993. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03602", "source_id": "AP03602", "source_numeric_id": "03602", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03602", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Flow-Based Fmoc-SPPS Preparation and SAR Study of Cathelicidin-PY Reveals Selective Antimicrobial Activity.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
